# tlo: wykopki
# rozdzial: Chapter Seven
# tytul: Whitsun
After the harvest the gossamer of late summer drifted for a long while over the stubble in silver threads, and every morning the cobwebs on the fences were hung with drops of dew like strings of beads.
In September the potatoes were dug. The whole village went out into the fields then with hoes and baskets, and after dark bonfires of dry haulm burned along the field balks. The children roasted potatoes in the embers and ate them straight from the ashes, scalding their fingers, while the grown-ups sat by the fire and told how things had been in their young days. Jaromir loved those evenings more than any others. The smoke stung his eyes, the earth smelled of cold, and when he lifted his head the stars were already shining above the forest – sharp and chill as splinters of ice. # pokaz: zmrok
In October the cabbage was pickled. The women shredded great heaps of it on a table in front of the cottage, and the men trod it down in barrels with their bare feet until the juice came up to their ankles. Mother sprinkled caraway over every layer and threw in a handful of cranberries, “so the sauerkraut won’t be afraid of the winter”.{ blizna_sierpa: When the first frosts came, the scar on Jaromir’s {miejsce_blizny()} began to ache – dully, stubbornly, always at the same hour, at noon exactly.} # dalej
