# tlo: wielkanoc
In March a warm wind blew from the south and in a single night licked the snow off the fields. The marshes swelled, the footbridge by the shrine went under water, and the ice on the lake broke up with a roar so loud that people ran out in front of their cottages. # pokaz: lod
For Easter Mother baked yeast cakes so tall they barely fitted in the oven, and Jaromir carried a basket to church to be blessed, with eggs dyed in onion skins, a piece of sausage, bread and horseradish. On the Monday the boys drenched the girls with water from the well – he soaked Hanka from head to foot, and she chased him with a bucket all the way to the lake and doused him so thoroughly that he sneezed for a week. # pokaz: dyngus
After the holidays the sawmill started up again. The screech of the saw came back, and with it the carts loaded with trunks. Jaromir was fourteen now, and for the first time he noticed that his father had begun to ask his opinion. # dalej
