# tlo: jezioro_swiatki
In the evening the young people gathered by the lake. It was done so every year: the boys lit a bonfire on the sandy spit, the girls set wreaths afloat on the water with little burning splints in them, and whoever found a wreath washed up on the shore knew whom they would go to the altar with. The fire crackled and showered sparks, there was a smell of smoke and wet rushes, and the girls’ laughter carried over the water. # pokaz: wianki
Even the boys from Bukowiec came, with Bartek, the miller’s son, at their head – strapping and noisy as ever – and they wagered on who could leap over the fire without singeing his breeches.
Apart from the others, on the jetty by the reeds, stood old Mrs Wójcik. For the third spring running she laid a crown of white water lilies on the lake – with no light at all – and watched for a long time as it drifted away. For Kaśka, people said. For the daughter the water never gave back. # pokaz: wojcikowa
Franek sat to one side, away from the flames. For a year something had been gnawing at him – { franek_scial_dab: ever since he felled the Old Oak, | ever since Urbaniak threw him out of the sawmill,} he went about sullen, lay awake at night and fell asleep on his feet by day. Now he crouched at the very edge of the water and stared into the rushes as doggedly as if he were searching for something there.
Antek did not leave his side for a moment. He sat two ells away, making a show of whittling a stick, and every little while he raised his head to check that his brother was still there.
When dusk fell and the bonfire burned low, singing drifted out of the reeds. # pokaz: spiew
It was soft and thin, like girls singing at the washing, but it had no words – only a melody, sad and sweet, that crept under the skin and drew you towards the water like a string.
Franek stood up.
“Do you hear?” he whispered. His face was radiant as a child’s. “They’re calling me. They’ve been calling me for a year.”
Before anyone could stop him, he walked into the water. # pokaz: franek # dalej
