    Yet they let Franek go. “Take him, then,” the one with the beads added. “The water won’t go to sleep hungry tonight anyway.” They drifted away slowly, backwards, never taking their black eyes off Franek, and sank one after another until only rings were left on the water. The last of them, before she vanished, whispered: “He’ll come back to us.” # pokaz: znikaja # dalej
