# tlo: brzeg_noc
Franek coughed up water for a long time. He was shaking all over, his teeth chattering with cold, and his hair was dripping, but he seemed not to feel it. Then he sat up, wiped his face and looked at them as if he were seeing them for the first time. # pokaz: franek
“Why did you pull me out?” he asked quietly. “It was so good down there. Warm, peaceful… and nobody wanted anything from me.”
Antek, plastered in mud up to the neck, grabbed him by his wet shirt and shook him like a sack.
“And Father? And Mother?” he croaked. “And Grandfather? Did you think of them?”
At last he let go of him, sat down in the mud beside him and wept in earnest, not pretending it was sweat or water.
