# tlo: bez_zachod
A week after Whitsun the old elder at the edge of the meadow bloomed so thickly that from afar it looked plastered with snow. Their old den still hung in its crown – rotting, its little roof full of holes, its ladder missing two rungs now.
Hanka was sitting at the very top, her legs tucked under her, when Jaromir climbed up to her. The sun was setting behind the lake, and the air smelled of elderflower so sweetly that your head swam – just as it had when they were children and hid here from storms. # pokaz: para
“Do you remember?” she asked, without looking at him. “The four of us used to fit in here.”
“I remember,” he said.
For a while they were silent.{ mak_w_medaliku: Hanka was toying with the locket at her throat, in which since last summer she had carried a dried poppy.}{ poszedl_po_wstazke && not wstazka_marzanny: In her hair was a red ribbon – the very one Jaromir had once gone into the forest to fetch.}
“I was afraid that time, at the lake,” she said at last, quietly. “Not of the rusalki – only that they’d pull you in too.”
