    He did not answer. He leaned over and kissed her – clumsily, quickly, barely brushing her lips. Hanka went still, then gave a short laugh, laid her head on his shoulder, and so they stayed until the first stars came out in the sky and her mother’s call carried from the meadow. # pokaz: pocalunek
*   [Take her hand and say nothing.]
    He could not find the words. He only took her hand – rough from work, warm – and held it until the sun went out behind the lake and the crickets began to chirp in the grass. Hanka did not draw her hand away. # pokaz: dlonie
